The original [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one known issue has one fix queued.
Its own rendered evidence contradicts that conclusion: the ticket combines a shared parser problem and a separate booking-form hint problem.
The counts below describe the supplied export. The subsequent engineering update reports the parser fixed and the hint issue closed without a fix because booking-v3 was retired.

<Callout kind="warn">
Triage by tenant configuration and entry channel, then verify symptoms. Matching subject lines alone is insufficient.
</Callout>

## Engineering update: 5 October

The [course desk update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) reports #4471 closed on 5 October.

- Parser: **fixed** — fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales. GitHub issue #1 is completed.
- Hint: **won’t fix** — booking-v3 form retired. GitHub issue #2 is not planned; the hint was not repaired.

These are the desk’s reported resolutions, not production changes made in this repository. The original export and its report counts remain historical evidence. The one-day observations remain unexplained by this update.

## Count the reports, not export rows or intake guesses

<ReviewSummary />

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table describes ownership in the exported support system. The separate GitHub tickets below track this review; creating them does not rewrite the export.

## Problems and separate tickets

### Shared parser reads month first

[GitHub issue #1](https://github.com/przemuh/mega-dev-kb/issues/1)

The shared parser assumes month/day even when the tenant's locale is day-first.
The supplied classifier assigns app and email reports from day-first tenants here, along with form reports using booking-v2.
For example, an intended 7 April becoming 4 July is a day/month swap.

Keep the parser fix separate from the form hint fix. Verify locale-aware parsing with ambiguous dates and unambiguous dates, and ensure app, email, and booking-v2 inputs agree.

### booking-v3 date hint conflicts with tenant locale

[GitHub issue #2](https://github.com/przemuh/mega-dev-kb/issues/2)

The booking-v3 form prints MM/DD/YYYY for day-first tenants, but reads the entered value using the tenant's day-first order.
People following that hint can get a swapped date even independently of the shared parser problem.
The supplied tenant directory identifies Alder Physio, Copper Studio, and Pale Harbour as booking-v3 tenants.

Make the visible hint and accepted input format agree with the tenant locale. Verify the displayed hint, actual submission, and saved date together.
App and email reports from these tenants still belong to the parser group; tenant identity alone is insufficient.

Ticket links and their report-ID membership are recorded in the repository's evidence directory. Counts in this page are computed from the current local data at render time.

## Arrival time is different from merge time

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The received series describes when reports reached the desk. The merged series describes when the desk put them into this ticket.
The July merge spike must not be presented as the incident's onset or a sudden rise in affected users.
These are report counts, not unique customer or user counts.

## Why the old triage guidance is unsafe

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) and the [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) were last reviewed in June 2024.
Their rendered stale banners matter: accepted status does not make their subject-only rule current.
The original decision remains intact as history. This review proposes replacing that rule with cause-aware triage after review by the support owner.

<DedupeExplorer />

The explorer shows both counterexamples: identical subjects can describe different causes, and different subjects can describe the same cause.
Unknown tenants require investigation; lack of a known cause is not evidence that two reports are duplicates.

## Evidence and refresh procedure

The analysis uses uniqueById, groupByCause, causeOf, and the tenant directory from this export.
The locale ordering comes from Intl.DateTimeFormat, not from browserLocale or a handwritten country list.
Keep the one-day observations visible while investigating; do not invent a timezone diagnosis.

When the desk supplies an update, replace the specified data files, recompute report membership, update the corresponding GitHub issues, and rebuild this page.
The repository contains both this .svx source and the HTML generated from it with the original components, including the signed desk reference below.

